@General_member_A: I’ve opened a Support ticket with your three items and the 9:15–9:30am ET timestamps; Support typically replies within 24–48 hours and may ask you for screenshots or network logs—I’ll post updates here as soon as they respond.  
@Enthusiast_member_B: For frequent travel try schedules tied to local events (e.g., sunrise +30 minutes) so “morning” follows local time, and add a small home geofence so weekday routines only run when you’re home; if you prefer a fixed timezone, keep a separate “home-time” schedule you enable when you arrive.  
@Basic_member_C: Since your app shows only an on/off, skip tonight by opening App → Schedules → [Evening] and flip the on/off switch to disable it, then manually run your preferred lights/thermostat settings or use the thermostat’s “Hold,” and flip the switch back on tomorrow (or set a reminder to re-enable); tell me if you want step‑by‑step screenshots.

@General_member_A: it’s fine to keep making reasonable edits—Support will use the timestamps you provided, so please note any further edits (time + timezone) rather than doing bulk changes while the ticket’s open.  
@Enthusiast_member_B: +30 min is a great baseline; in darker months try +45–60 min or create two travel presets (summer/winter) you switch between.  
@Basic_member_C: re‑enabling later is fine—the schedule will next run at its next scheduled time once turned back on and won’t retroactively trigger missed events.  
@General_member_E: to add a weekend-only scene go App → Schedules → Create (or +) → add your lighting actions → set active days to Sat & Sun only; this keeps your weekday schedule intact—happy to walk through screenshots if you want.

@General_member_A: this looked like a one‑off backend hiccup so you can keep editing as usual, but if anything else appears off please include the item names plus your app’s "Last sync" time (found in Settings → Account/About) when you report it.  
@Enthusiast_member_B: sunrise-based schedules (sunrise +30–60m) are still the best "set-and-forget" for frequent travel; if you prefer a fixed home rhythm later, keep a separate "home-time" preset you can switch to.  
@General_member_E: for a Vacation schedule avoid conflicts by giving it distinct active days or conditions (geofence or “only when home”), or temporarily disable your weekend/weekday schedules while Vacation is on—then test it once to confirm.  
If anyone wants step‑by‑step taps or screenshots to set/test these, reply here and I’ll walk you through them.

@General_member_A: you can generally trust the automatic background sync—use "Sync Now" only when you want edits pushed immediately or if you ever see a mismatch.  
@Enthusiast_member_B: I’d keep sunrise-based (sunrise +30–60m) for a natural feel and maintain a separate fixed "home-time" preset you switch to when you need strict predictability.  
@General_member_F: check Android Settings → Apps → [our app] → Notifications to ensure notifications (and the Schedule/Scene category) are allowed, disable battery optimizations/unrestricted background battery and allow background data, and verify Do Not Disturb isn’t blocking them.  
If notifications still miss, post your app "Last sync" time and a screenshot of the app’s notification settings here and I’ll help escalate.

@General_member_F: since you’ve checked the basics, also verify the app’s notification channel importance (Settings → Apps → [app] → Notifications → tap the Schedule/Scene category → set Importance to High/Urgent and disable “Show silently”) and check manufacturer battery managers (e.g., Device care → Battery → App power management on Samsung) to ensure the app isn’t marked as Sleeping/Restricted. If it still misses alerts, reproduce the next missed run and post the scheduled time, your app “Last sync” time, and screenshots of the app’s notification-channel and battery-management settings so I can escalate.  
@General_member_G: to copy a schedule, open App → Schedules → tap the schedule → menu (three dots) → Duplicate (if available), then rename and swap devices to the bedroom; if Duplicate isn’t present, export the actions into a Scene (App → Scenes → + → add same actions) and create a new weekday Schedule that runs that Scene.  
If either of you wants step‑by‑step screenshots, tell me which phone model and I’ll post them.

@General_member_F: scheduled runs should normally produce the same notification as a manual trigger when notifications are enabled—please reproduce the next missed run and post the scheduled run time (e.g., 6:17pm), your app “Last sync” time, plus screenshots of Settings → Apps → [our app] → Notifications (tap the Schedule/Scene channel) and your phone’s Battery/App power management so we can check for OS suppression and escalate with logs.  
@General_member_G: to turn the living‑room schedule into a reusable Scene, open App → Schedules → tap the living‑room schedule and note its actions, then go App → Scenes → + (Create Scene) → Add the same device actions and Save; to make the bedroom schedule go App → Schedules → + → name it → set days/time → Add action → Run Scene → select your new Scene → Save.  
If either of you wants, tell me your phone model and I’ll post step‑by‑step screenshots.
